  "title": "somatomotor",
  "description": "This dataset comprises multi-subject, multi-modal neuroimaging recordings (structural MRI, MEG, and EEG) collected during a median nerve stimulation paradigm. Participants received electrical stimuli to the right wrist median nerve and responded by lifting their left index finger as quickly as possible. The dataset supports investigation of somatosensory and motor cortical responses using combined MEG/EEG/MRI methodology.",
  "methods_description": "MRI (T1w), MEG, and EEG data were acquired while median nerve electrical stimuli were delivered at the right wrist, and subjects responded by lifting their left hand index finger. Three anatomical fiducials (nasion, left and right pre-auricular points) were digitized to co-register MEG with MRI. Trigger codes recorded stimulus (32) and response (16) events.",
